Nuclear fusion powers the stars. The core reaction for deuterium-tritium (D-T) fusion:
  ²H + ³H → ⁴He (3.5 MeV) + n (14.1 MeV)

Total energy released: Q = Δm·c²
Where Δm = (m_D + m_T) - (m_He + m_n)
         = (2.01410 + 3.01605) - (4.00260 + 1.00867) u
         = 0.01888 u
         = 0.01888 × 931.5 MeV/u
         = 17.59 MeV per fusion event

